// Electron runtime args for VS Code.
// password-store: "basic" = unencrypted plaintext file under ~/.config/Code.
// Chosen explicitly over gnome-libsecret because gnome-keyring 50's V0
// collection-exposure bug (see fixes/vscode-keyring-gnome-keyring-50.md)
// causes Electron's libsecret probe to fail on this machine even with
// the daemon running and PAM-unlocked. Setting "basic" here pre-empts the
// auto-detect failure dialog.
//
// The secrets VS Code stores (OAuth session tokens for GitHub / Copilot,
// MCP creds) are all revocable and already live in memory plaintext
// while VS Code runs — encryption at rest would defend against offline
// disk access only.
{
  "password-store": "basic"
}
